the number is *not* divisible by $6$ either.\n\n- If we substitute $9$ into the blank, we get $11\\,521\\,696,$ which is divisible by $2.$ However, it is not divisible by $3$ because the sum of the digits is $22+9=31,$ which is not divisible by $3.$ So, the number is *not* divisible by $6$ either.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172311 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171933 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b483f9f7-47a9-5725-b1f1-fe0ea39a7e96" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Number Is Divisible by 6"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca7235df-ed54-56b4-a96a-f4dd62411d9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168730} {:answer/id #uuid "09345208-4c96-5ff8-aad9-4dc79f7055c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168731} {:answer/id #uuid "3f01a342-66a4-565d-8547-c05a295e8ace" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168732} {:answer/id #uuid "48110931-110b-5b28-8961-d5731a2dc0ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168733} {:answer/id #uuid "4b893675-cde8-51e7-879a-c1367e13459f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168734}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b893675-cde8-51e7-879a-c1367e13459f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168734} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4005020-e950-5306-a22c-5bc62b40c40b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168729}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c81002d7-9f3e-57b8-8938-1545e4037d2f" :question/math-academy-id "q-132404" :question/problem "Which digits, when inserted into the blank, make the number $66\\,333\\,9◻0$ divisible by $6?$\n\nI. $0$\n\nII. $3$\n\nIII. $9$" :question/worked-solution "A number is divisible by $6$ if it is divisible by both $2$ and $3.$ Remember that to determine whether a number is divisible by $3,$ we check whether the sum of the digits is divisible by $3.$\n\nFor the given number, the sum of the digits is\n\n$$\n6+6+3+3+3+9+◻+0=30+◻.\n$$\n\nNow, let's consider each of the given digits we can substitute into the blank.\n\n- If we substitute $0$ into the blank, we get $66\\,333\\,900,$ which is divisible by $2.$ Then the sum of the digits is $30+0=30,$ which is divisible by $3,$ so the number is also divisible by $3.$ Therefore, the number is divisible by $6.$\n\n- If we substitute $3$ into the blank, we get $66\\,333\\,930,$ which is divisible by $2.$ Then the sum of the digits is $30+3=33,$ which is divisible by $3,$ so the number is also divisible by $3.$ Therefore, the number is divisible by $6.$\n\n- If we substitute $9$ into the blank, we get $66\\,333\\,990,$ which is divisible by $2.$ Then the sum of the digits is $30+9=39,$ which is divisible by $3,$ so the number is also divisible by $3.$ Therefore, the number is divisible by $6.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}]}
